# 0.0.7 over 0.0.6: no API change; calls do not change. It moves to
# nightly-2026-11-15-f25da45, which warns when a local or a nested member has the
# name of a top-level definition, so three names moved: `Protocol.new` takes
# `limit` (was `max_message`), `Session.start!` takes `first_link` (was `link`),
# and `Server.Request` is now an alias of a top-level type `ServerRequest`
# (`Request(b, e) : ServerRequest(b, e)`) that carries its methods, because its
# method `accept!` has the name of `Server.accept!`. An app still writes
# `request.accept!(...)` and `Server.Request` in annotations; the topics and the
# overview needed no change beyond the URLs.
#
# 0.0.6 over 0.0.5: no API change. It moves to nightly-2026-11-07-ad3a5d2
# (`Stream.custom` takes `Err(Unknown)`, so it does not build on an older
# nightly), and documents `poll!` as an idle deadline (any frame restarts it)
# and `ReceiveWithin` as a total one. The overview's feature table and
# ws_client say so.
#
# 0.0.5 over 0.0.4, breaking for code that runs handlers: `Ws.Handlers.on_close!`
# gets the connection (`|state, conn, closure|`), `Ws.drive!` returns
# `(state, ended)` and no longer a `Try`, a handler's `Err(Closed)` no longer
# ends the run, and the echo of the peer's Close waits until the messages read
# with it are delivered. Added: the `Server` module (the server driver over
# bytes: `Server.accept!`, `Server.read_request!`, `Server.Request`,
# `Server.Conn`, `Server.ops`, `Server.Transport`), `Ws.Upgrade`, `Ws.Refusal`,
# `Handshake.refusal`, `Handshake.head_end` and `Protocol.expects`;
# `Handshake.choose_protocol` picks by the server's order. 0.0.4 added
# `Client.Conn.map_link`. 0.0.3 renamed Ws.Dial to Ws.Connect, Ws.Request to
# Ws.ConnectRequest and Client.Link to Client.Transport, made Client.Conn opaque
# and made `poll!` give `TimedOut`. The overview names those old spellings,
# because a model recalls them.

index.json  <- package/ (src/), parsed by `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. Public
               and private modules; `package [...]` in src/main.roc is what
               separates them. No source is vendored
examples/   <- examples/sans_io.roc and echo_server.roc, repinned with two edits per file. Upstream pins the
               package as `pkg: "../src/main.roc"`, a path that resolves only inside a
               checkout, so the header's entry is replaced with the 0.0.7
               tarball above under the name `ws` (and `import pkg.X` with
               `import ws.X`); and the file gains one `##`
               line above its header, because that line is the title
               `list_roc_index(kind: "examples")` prints. Nothing else differs.
topics/     <- this package's own, not upstream's: programs written against
               this pin. ws_client and ws_server use the roc-basic-cli-websocket
               adapter (below). ws_adapters and ws_frames use no platform I/O.
overview.md <- this package's own. Every API claim on it was compiled, and every
               fenced block appears in verify/overview-snippets.roc.

